===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[review]] or a [[revision]].
# {{lb|en|printing}} A second proof sheet; a proof sheet taken after the first or a subsequent correction.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1837|author=Anthony Panizzi|title=A letter to His Royal Highness the President of the Royal Society, on the New Catalogue of the Library of that Institution Now in the Press|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=i5MIAAAAQAAJ&pg=PA30&dq=%22the+revises%22+-intitle:%22revises%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=t60KULD_EfGPiAeistG1DQ&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22the%20revises%22%20-intitle%3A%22revises%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false|page=30
|passage=The question is, not whether the '''revises''' of the Catalogue, which I was obliged to circulate prematurely, were faultless, but whether the alterations which I was desired to make would not render them worse.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1997|author=w:David Lodge|title=The Practice of Writing|pageurl=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=gWSQw05Y3qMC&pg=PA219&dq=%22the+revises%22+-intitle:%22revises%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=EMgKUN-eM-iQiAftwqW0DQ&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22the%20revises%22%20-intitle%3A%22revises%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false|page=219|year_published=2011
|passage={{...}}until I had corrected the proofs of the novel and seen the '''revises''', so that the text was irrevocably fixed, before beginning the screenplay.}}

